docs/PERF-2026-07-23.md:292:| **B2. Drop fragments with support < `min_corr_pts` before scoring** | ≥50 % of the candidate scan disappears; plausibly the single largest remaining win after F1 | `buildFragGrid` builds `g.rt` as the union of *surviving* fragment RTs, and `G = |g.rt|` enters both Pearson denominators (`:1109`, `:460-462`) and decides where precursor points snap (`:1090-1098`). Identical **iff** every window frame still contributes ≥1 retained peak — unmeasured. **Gate on a `|unique g.rt| == wmap.size()` counter first.** The safe form is `if (fg.supEnd(fi) - fg.supBegin(fi) < min_corr_pts) continue;` immediately before the dot loop at `:1121`: no grid change, no index remap, provably identical — but it saves only the dot product, not the tracing. |
docs/PERF-2026-07-23.md:293:| **B3. Raise `trace:ms2_min_length_sec` above 0** | kills the single-point traces at the source, i.e. B2's win *plus* the tracing and EPD cost | Deletes traces. Direct recall risk. |
docs/PERF-2026-07-23.md:294:| **B4. `trace:termination_outliers` < 5** | fewer wasted extension steps at both ends of every trace | Changes where traces terminate and how often two peaks merge. |
