docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:133:  // detectTraces_ distributes its bands as TASKS, which requires an enclosing parallel region;
docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:135:- **Performance:** `src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:2506-2510` shows banding **reduces total CPU** (11,168 → 2,972 s across 5/12/24 bands) because MassTraceDetection's cost is **superlinear** in peak count.
docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:138:  - Banding is **not needed to fill cores** (task pool handles that)
docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:141:  - **Cost:** No loss of parallelism; bands are tasks in the pool
docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:144:**Answer:** Yes. The master/worker task pool (`src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:1074-1075`, `src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:2030-2040`) already decouples parallelism from banding. Bands are now **performance optimization**, not **parallelism mechanism**.
docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:156:| **Measure error?** | **Jaccard vs unbanded** on stratified window sample; report symmetric difference. |
docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:157:| **Parallelism without partition?** | **Yes** — task pool already supports it; bands are for performance, not parallelism. |
