docs/reviews/backlog-2026-09-02-codex.md:1:1. **Blocker — B2 must precede landing A1.** The plan merges the parallel loader before diagnosing why batch 64 and 256 allegedly produce different content ([analysis:79–80](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtract/docs/BACKLOG-ANALYSIS-2026-09-02.md:79)). The stated exclusions are invalid: `const` does not prove library purity; absence of pointer-ordered containers in this file says nothing about OpenMS/opentims; and batch size changes OpenMP concurrency and which threads call `get_frame`, `decompress`, `save_to_buffs`, and `frame.close()` on one shared handle ([patch:209–240](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtract/patches/openms-brukertims-mz-calibration.patch:209)). Test batch 64 versus 256 at one thread, then 100 threads; checksum raw per-frame `(scan,intensity,mz,IM)` arrays before sorting/picking; then compare post-pick spectra. Correction: make B2 plan item 1 and prohibit A1 merge until raw-frame and stage digests identify or eliminate loader corruption.
docs/reviews/backlog-2026-09-02-codex.md:17:9. **Major — the active inventory misses R4 and the unresolved PTM ambiguity.** Double-scoring 2.99% of overlapping-window precursors remains an hours-scale 2–3% runtime item ([RUNTIME-QUALITY:21](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtract/docs/RUNTIME-QUALITY-ASSESSMENT-2026-07-27.md:21); [PROJECT-REVIEW:66–67](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtract/docs/PROJECT-REVIEW-2026-09-01.md:66)). The table-model result also leaves a 34.7%-versus-14% known-PTM ambiguity and an uninvestigated 1,610-unit Amidation bin ([S30-BASELINE:303–311](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtract/docs/S30-BASELINE.md:303)). Correction: add both as explicit open rows.
