docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:2:• This is a substantial review task. I need to read the specified files first. Let me read them in parallel. The main C++ file is likely large. Let me start.
docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:10:  This is a big reading task. Plan: read the rest of DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp (lines 1001-2864) directly, and page through the saved outputs for the elided middle parts. Given context limits, maybe delegate parts to subagents. But the review quality depends on me seeing the code. Total remaining: ~1800 lines of C++ (~60KB), ~63KB of S30-BASELINE middle, ~70KB of the first-1000 C++ elided middle.
docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:32:  Also README build instructions: `build/DIAPseudoSpectra` but CMakeLists doesn't show how to build standalone beyond `cmake -DOpenMS_DIR=...`. README says "then rebuild the OpenMS DIAPseudoSpectra target" — contradictory with "standalone application, lives outside the OpenMS source tree"! The README Build section says apply patches to OpenMS and "rebuild the OpenMS DIAPseudoSpectra target" — but the tool is standalone per CMakeLists comment. That's an inconsistency worth flagging: the apply_openms_patches.sh installs src/TdfMzCalibration.h + patches into OpenMS; but where does DIAPseudoSpectra get built? CMakeLists exists for standalone. README never gives the actual cmake commands for building this repo. Gap.
docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:38:  1. `winKey` quantization: `(int)llround(lo*100.0)` then `win_lo = key.first / 100.0`. Isolation window boundaries quantized to 0.01 Da. Two distinct windows whose lo/hi round to the same centi-Da get merged — probably fine. But more subtle: the precursor's mono_mz window membership uses quantized win_lo/win_hi vs the original lo/hi used for routing. A precursor at the true window edge could be routed differently... Actually routing of frames uses keyfn_(lo,hi) on the actual frame's isolation window; windows come from the data, so consistent. Precursor membership: `plo/phi` from prec_mz within [win_lo, win_hi] — quantized boundaries differ from true by ≤0.005 Da; a precursor within 5 mDa of a window edge could be included/excluded incorrectly vs the fragment routing. Minor; also asymmetric: precursor in window but its fragments routed by true window. Minor finding.
docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:68:  8. The window loop: `win_out[wi]` per-window bucket, no data race. pdense firstprivate in inner precursor loop. `t_mat` etc. atomics. `fanout_hist` under critical. Looks OK. One issue: in the apportion and rp_max branches, the precursor loops are SERIAL within the window (no inner parallel) — fine.
docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:74:  9. `#pragma omp critical` without name in several places (det digest, win_done, worker_err, pick_err in main_) — unnamed criticals all share one global lock; correctness fine.
docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:76:  10. Memory admission: `inflight += need` under critical(admit); Release destructor `c -= n` — if an exception is thrown inside the try after Release constructed... Release is a local struct in the try block; exception caught by catch(...) in same loop iteration — destructor runs during unwind. OK. But note: the Release is constructed AFTER the admission loop; if materializeWindow throws, rel destructs — fine.
docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:88:  14. `exact()`: `tof = llround((sqrt(v) - c0)/c1)` — for v≤0, sqrt NaN → llround NaN UB (same class of bug they fixed in compactify!). `if (std::isfinite(e)) v = e;` guards the output but not the llround input. Peaks with mz>0 from archive presumably; but the exact() path: mz from sp.mz() are positive. Minor.
docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:106:  Also for question 2: "parameters documented as FALSIFIED still exist with the defaults the docs claim" — rp_max default 0 ✓ exists; consolidate:delta_rt 0 ✓; merge:rt_window 0 ✓; apportion exists default 0 ✓ (help doesn't say FALSIFIED though! CHANGELOG says "Help texts of falsified flags (rp_max, consolidate, merge) now say so" — apportion falsified again 2026-09-02 (E5, -3.9%) but its help string does NOT say FALSIFIED — it says "Try 1 (linear) or 2 (sharper)". That's a stale help string: apportion was cleanly falsified (-3.9%) yet the help still invites the user to try it. Good finding.
docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:108:  Also `assembly:rank_by` intensity — is it falsified? Not stated. `charge:ambiguity_margin` falsified per README ("Left at 0") but help string doesn't say FALSIFIED — says "0 = single charge per precursor". README documents falsification with table. Help could say so but doesn't — minor inconsistency. Also `trace:wavelet_smooth` — status? Docs? Probably falsified or under test; help says "Try 0.25-0.5" — need to check S30-BASELINE for wavelet verdict.
docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:116:  Env vars in code: SPEXTRACT_DROP_PREC_ISO, SPEXTRACT_MZ_ESTIMATOR, SPEXTRACT_DET, SPEXTRACT_PICK_SERIAL, SPEXTRACT_PICK_STATIC, SPEXTRACT_PICK_BATCH, SPEXTRACT_PICK_MZ_MODE, SPEXTRACT_LOAD_ONLY, SPEXTRACT_MIN_ISOTOPES, SPEXTRACT_PRECURSOR_LIST, SPEXTRACT_MZPEAK_EXACT, SPEXTRACT_MZPEAK_TDF, SPEXTRACT_ALLOW_CHORD_FALLBACK (in TdfMzCalibration.h presumably), SPEXTRACT_BACKFILL_RAW?, SPEXTRACT_ISO_COLLAPSE? Need grep.
