docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:122:  2. The task's question 2 asks: "is charge:min_charge really applied where the docs say (after the isotope-support gate, before extraction, and NOT dropping charge-0/'guessed' precursors)?" Code: gate order in main_: default_charge assignment (2032-2033) → require_isotope_support (2037) → min_charge (2051-2058) → before window loop/extraction. Predicate `pc.charge > 0 && pc.charge < zmin` → charge-0 (open_search_safe) NOT dropped ✓. But subtle: with open_search_safe OFF, guessed precursors were assigned default_charge=2 BEFORE the min_charge gate, so they survive ✓. With default_charge=0 and open_search_safe off: charge stays 0? Code: `pc.charge = open_safe ? 0 : default_charge;` → default_charge=0 → charge 0 → survives min_charge, emitted with charge unset. Docs? "0 = leave charge UNSET". OK consistent.
