docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/kimi.err:215:  But hold on — this assumes trace CPU really halves on S08 with 24 bands (S30 measurement) and that admission/fill behave. And 24 bands × halo on narrow windows: comment says narrow tile (19 Da) at 24 bands = 57% halo overhead — but that overhead is included in the S30 CPU measurement presumably (S30 also has 24 windows...). The per-window width-derived band heuristic was REJECTED in favour of flat 12 (:2376-2380). Flat 24 lost on WALL at 8×24=192 threads oversubscribed — but with n_conc=4 it's 96 threads. The existing option pins bands and auto-derives n_conc = 100/24 = 4. So the A/B is literally `-perf:trace_bands 24`. Also intermediate: 6×16=96. Test all.
