docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/kimi.err:333:  Also small: `schedule(dynamic)` outer loop with admission INSIDE the iteration means a thread holding a big window blocks others from... no, dynamic gives each thread next window when free; admission may make a thread wait while others could take smaller windows that fit — head-of-line blocking: a thread stuck waiting for a 50 GB need blocks its slot even though a later small window would fit. With heavy-first + dynamic, iteration order is fixed (heavy→light); waiting threads each hold a specific wi. Minor: could re-order to "admit any window that fits" (work-stealing by size). Small gain; mention under R6.
