docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/codex.transcript:2150:The implementation already contradicts its own exactness claim at the relevant boundary: detection uses the full `MassTrace` centroid for ownership, but the data supplied to that detector has already been clipped to a finite halo. I’m now checking the actual OpenMS trace-growth implementation, because the running-centroid recurrence and visited/occupancy semantics determine whether the proposed counterexamples are genuinely executable rather than merely intuitive.
