docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/codex.transcript:2267:/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtract/src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:876:    registerDoubleOption_("trace:max_trace_length_sec", "<sec>", -1.0, "DANGER - NOT a guard. MassTraceDetection::isTraceValid_ RETURNS FALSE on over-length traces and peaks are marked visited only for VALID traces, so an over-length blob is rejected, re-seeded by the next apex, and rejected again - emitting NOTHING at that m/z. Setting this DELETES signal (the falsified direction). Kept only for diagnostics; leave at -1. Splitting requires ElutionPeakDetection, not this. [merged-trace]", false, true);
