  1219	    registerDoubleOption_("trace:wavelet_smooth", "<x>", 0.0, "[wavelet] Smooth the PRECURSOR XIC with a stationary (a-trous) B3-spline wavelet before correlating fragments against it, at a scale of x TIMES THE MEASURED MS1 FWHM. diaTracer smooths its precursor profile (2D Gaussian + Savitzky-Golay) and then applies a 0.3 correlation threshold; we copied the 0.3 but not the smoothing. Pearson r between two NOISY profiles is attenuated toward 0 as S/N falls, so an unsmoothed 0.3 is a systematically weaker constraint than a smoothed 0.3 -- and worst at faint precursors, which is where the coverage analysis says peptides are lost. Fragment XICs stay RAW (as in diaTracer) and emitted peak intensities are unaffected. 0 = off. Try 0.25-0.5 (measured MS1 FWHM is 3.61 s on S30, so 0.5 ~ 1.8 s ~ 1.3 cycles).", false);
