docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/kimi.err-287-  One more faithfulness item: OpenMS `findBestPeak_` non-IM... n/a, IM present. Also OpenMS requires candidate within ±3*ftl_sd where ftl_sd REESTIMATED robustly — important: the initial ftl_sd = centroid*ppm/1e6, so ±3×20ppm = ±60ppm initially, tightening as the trace gathers points. So OpenMS's window is typically WIDER than the integer span early and possibly narrower later. Also reestimate can make sd very small for clean traces → window collapses to ~3× observed scatter. Integer: fixed ~ppm/2-relative bins... wait: span in TOF bins for a relative m/z tolerance: m ∝ tof², dm/m = 2 dtof/tof → dtof = tof × ppm/2e6. The design says "a relative m/z tolerance is about half of it in tof". ax.span converts mz(1+ppm) both ends — correct.
