docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/kimi.err-304-  8. Noise-floor membership: integer extension takes peaks ≤ noise (OpenMS work_exp excludes them) → centroids dragged, sample-rate denominators change. Symptom: traces lengthen into noise, RT tails, FragGrid correlation diluted.
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/kimi.err-305-  9. Uniform-width TOF bands vs quantile bands — peak density in TOF space is highly non-uniform; one band gets most peaks; the superlinear candidate-scan term concentrates there → wall time worse and nondeterministic-ish scheduling. Performance, not correctness.
