docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/kimi.err-336-  Also for Q1: one more OpenMS behavior — `chrom_apices` built from peaks > snr*noise, but EXTENSION candidate peaks only need > noise. Integer matches this for seeds but NOT for members (no noise filter in pick). Covered. Also OpenMS marks apex visited only if trace valid — integer marks at seed time. Covered. Also OpenMS `peak_visited` checked in isPeakAcceptable_ — same. Also OpenMS: when candidate found but not acceptable (used), it counts as a MISS (consecutive_missed++) — integer pick() skips used and returns next-best unused; if none unused within span → miss. Equivalent-ish. But subtle: OpenMS findBestPeak_ picks closest m/z peak within IM tol, then if it's USED → miss, even if an unused peak is also in the window! Integer pick() takes the closest UNUSED. Different membership decisions in contested windows: OpenMS wastes the frame (miss) when the best peak is taken; integer takes the second-best. That changes traces AND termination counts. Good catch — add to Q1 list. In dense regions this matters a lot.
