docs/INTEGER-TRACING-DESIGN.md-6-**What it runs on today.** `materializeWindow()` rebuilds an OpenMS `PeakMap` from the compact store:
docs/INTEGER-TRACING-DESIGN.md-7-`Peak1D` (double m/z + float intensity) plus a parallel `FloatDataArray` of mobility, wrapped in an
docs/INTEGER-TRACING-DESIGN.md-8-`MSSpectrum` per frame -- ~20 B/peak against the store's 10 B, plus per-spectrum object overhead,
docs/INTEGER-TRACING-DESIGN.md-9-and every m/z is a double that was an integer twice over (a TOF bin, then a 1e-5 Da store index).
docs/INTEGER-TRACING-DESIGN.md-10-`MassTraceDetection` then matches by a ppm tolerance on those doubles.
docs/INTEGER-TRACING-DESIGN.md-11-
